    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=\nEvaluate the beginner lesson below.\n\nTOPIC: Introduction to RAG\n\nLEARNER:\nA 12th-grade graduate from India.\nLimited English vocabulary.\nNo technical background.\n\nLESSON:\n{{ $json.current_lesson }}\n\nEvaluate the lesson using the six hard pass/fail checks below.\n\nCHECK 1 — ACCURACY AND GROUNDING\nPASS only if the lesson explains RAG correctly and does not claim\nthat RAG guarantees truth or prevents all hallucinations.\nCheck that examples do not present invented information as fact.\n\nCHECK 2 — BEGINNER-FRIENDLY LANGUAGE\nPASS only if a learner with no technical background can\nunderstand the lesson using simple English and short sentences.\n\nCHECK 3 — TEACHES BY EXAMPLE\nPASS only if the lesson includes a familiar example that\nexplains how RAG finds information and uses it to answer.\n\nCHECK 4 — NO UNEXPLAINED JARGON\nPASS only if technical terms are explained in simple words\nbefore or when they are first used.\n\nCHECK 5 — KEY POINTS COVERED\nPASS only if the lesson explains:\n- What RAG is.\n- Why RAG is useful.\n- How RAG works step by step.\n- How documents are prepared and searched.\n- How the AI uses retrieved information to answer.\n\nCHECK 6 — CLEAR TEACHING FLOW\nPASS only if the lesson moves logically from basic ideas\nto the process, example, and recap.\n\nIMPORTANT RULES:\n- Each check must be PASS or FAIL.\n- No partial credit.\n- Do not approve a lesson if any check fails.\n- Give a specific reason for every failed check.\n- Suggest a concrete correction for each failure.\n- Do not rewrite the lesson yourself.\n\nReturn:\n1. Overall decision: PASS or FAIL.\n2. Results for all six checks.\n3. Reasons for failures.\n4. Specific corrections needed.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a strict evaluator agent in a self-evaluating educational content system.\n\nYour job is to evaluate a beginner lesson against six hard pass/fail checks and return a structured decision.\n\nApply each check strictly with no partial credit. Do not approve a lesson if any check fails. Give a specific reason and a concrete correction for every failed check. Do not rewrite the lesson yourself."
        }
      },
      "id": "97f5c670-e295-4f0d-aad9-b557f9f7f92a",
